From: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: mtk-usxgmii: avoid link-up reset in USXGMII mode

The PCS link-up callback resets and reconfigures the USXGMII PCS and XFI
PHY immediately after phylink observes a successful in-band link. With
an Aeonsemi AS21010 PHY, the line-side autonegotiation remains complete
while the MediaTek PCS carrier repeatedly drops after this reset.

USXGMII already negotiates and reports its link state in-band, and the
PCS has been configured before link-up. Do not tear down that established
link from the link-up callback. Keep the existing reset sequence for the
fixed-rate 5GBASE-R and 10GBASE-R modes.

Signed-off-by: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
---
 drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-usxgmii.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-usxgmii.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-usxgmii.c
@@ -360,6 +360,9 @@ static void mtk_usxgmii_pcs_link_up(stru
 {
 	struct mtk_usxgmii_pcs *mpcs = pcs_to_mtk_usxgmii_pcs(pcs);
 
+	if (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII)
+		return;
+
 	/* Reconfiguring USXGMII to ensure the quality of the RX signal
 	 * after the line side link up.
 	 */
